    "summary": "libgcrypt is a general-purpose cryptographic library organized around a core runtime (global init, FIPS mode, secure memory, hardware feature detection) that dispatches to pluggable algorithm modules. The cipher subsystem provides symmetric ciphers with extensive hardware-accelerated implementations (AES-NI, NEON, AVX2/512, POWER, RISC-V, s390x) and multiple modes of operation (GCM, CCM, OCB, XTS, etc.). Hash and MAC modules support all major algorithms with similar platform optimizations. Public-key cryptography builds on a multi-precision integer (MPI) library with assembly backends for 15+ architectures, supporting RSA, DSA, ECC (including EdDSA/ECDH), plus post-quantum algorithms (ML-KEM/Kyber, ML-DSA/Dilithium, Classic McEliece, NTRU Prime). The random subsystem provides CSPRNG and DRBG implementations fed by multiple entropy sources including jitter entropy. The library exposes a stable C API through carefully controlled symbol visibility and includes a comprehensive test suite, autotools build system, and Texinfo documentation."
  },
